---
layout: default
---
<div class="nb">
  <header class="nb-hero">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Pocket brain · Graph mind map</p>
      <h1>Embrace <em>your</em> brain.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        n-brace is a free, offline-first app for visualizing and navigating your notes as a graph. Follow links instead of folders, and
        see which topic a note belongs to at a glance.
      </p>
      <div class="cta">
        <a class="btn-nb primary" href="{{ '/projects/nbrace_app/' | relative_url }}">Download the app</a>
        <a class="btn-nb secondary" href="{{ '/blog/' | relative_url }}">Read the knowledge base</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="shot">
      <img
        src="{{ '/assets/img/landing/hero.webp' | relative_url }}"
        alt="n-brace showing a recipe graph with colored tag regions"
        width="1600"
        height="859"
        fetchpriority="high"
      >
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="nb-facts">
    <span><b>Free</b> standalone app</span>
    <span><b>Windows</b> · macOS · Linux</span>
    <span><b>Offline-first</b>, your notes stay on your machine</span>
    <span><b>MCP</b> server for Claude</span>
  </div>

  <section class="nb-feats">
    <h2>Move through your notes instead of digging for them.</h2>

    <article class="nb-feat">
      <div class="txt">
        <p class="k">Navigate</p>
        <h3>Seamless navigation</h3>
        <p>
          Show only the local part of the graph you are exploring. Move through linked notes, jump between nodes with keyboard
          shortcuts, and let automatic layout keep everything readable.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="nb-media">
        <img
          src="{{ '/assets/img/landing/navigation.webp' | relative_url }}"
          alt="Graph of recipe notes centered on Lazy Dumplings"
          loading="lazy"
          width="1400"
          height="898"
        >
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="nb-feat">
      <div class="txt">
        <p class="k">Edit</p>
        <h3>Quick graph manipulation</h3>
        <p>
          A radial pie menu puts create, link, group and move actions one click away, right where your cursor is. Reshaping the map
          never breaks your flow.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="nb-media narrow">
        <img
          src="{{ '/assets/img/landing/pie-menu.webp' | relative_url }}"
          alt="Radial pie menu: zoom, add, edit and go to tag"
          loading="lazy"
          width="600"
          height="540"
        >
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="nb-feat">
      <div class="txt">
        <p class="k">See</p>
        <h3>Tag area view layer</h3>
        <p>
          Tags render as colored regions overlaid on the canvas, so you see at a glance which cluster or topic a note belongs to.
          Filter the view down to just the layers you care about.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="nb-media">
        <img
          src="{{ '/assets/img/landing/tags.webp' | relative_url }}"
          alt="Tag scope bar and colored tag regions behind the graph"
          loading="lazy"
          width="1120"
          height="840"
        >
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="nb-feat stack">
      <div class="txt">
        <p class="k">Structure</p>
        <h3>Deep structure</h3>
        <p>
          A note can have many flavors and contextual contents. Pizza sits in the whole recipe graph, while the ingredients layer
          shows only what it is made of. Deep, cross-cutting structures emerge from a flat graph.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="nb-pair">
        <div class="nb-media">
          <img
            src="{{ '/assets/img/landing/deep-pizza.webp' | relative_url }}"
            alt="Pizza and its ingredients with the ingredients tag area highlighted"
            loading="lazy"
            width="1000"
            height="1007"
          >
        </div>
        <div class="nb-media">
          <img
            src="{{ '/assets/img/landing/deep-ingredients.webp' | relative_url }}"
            alt="The ingredients layer on its own, centered on dairy"
            loading="lazy"
            width="1000"
            height="1033"
          >
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="nb-feat">
      <div class="txt">
        <p class="k">Remember</p>
        <h3>Reminders</h3>
        <p>
          Set reminders on any note to resurface repeating tasks, refresh knowledge you don't want to forget, or manage household
          chores, right from your graph.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="nb-media narrow">
        <img
          src="{{ '/assets/img/landing/reminders.webp' | relative_url }}"
          alt="House cleaning reminders with repeat schedules and progress counters"
          loading="lazy"
          width="778"
          height="1175"
        >
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="nb-feat stack">
      <div class="txt">
        <p class="k">Connect</p>
        <h3>MCP server for AI</h3>
        <p>
          A built-in <a href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MCP</a> server exposes your note graph
          to assistants like Claude Desktop and Claude Code. They can search your notes and import web articles as structured, tagged
          nodes.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="nb-media scroll-x">
        <img
          src="{{ '/assets/img/landing/mcp.webp' | relative_url }}"
          alt="Claude Code adding a microservices subtree of 38 notes to n-brace through the MCP server"
          loading="lazy"
          width="1438"
          height="453"
        >
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="nb-news">
    <h2><a href="{{ '/news/' | relative_url }}">News</a></h2>
    {% include news.liquid limit=true %}
  </section>

  <section class="nb-support">
    <div>
      <h2>Free, and in active development.</h2>
      <p>If you find n-brace useful, you can sponsor the project. Free hugs for all supporters ☕🤗</p>
    </div>
    <a class="btn-nb primary" href="https://buymeacoffee.com/nbrace" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sponsor on Buy Me a Coffee</a>
  </section>
</div>
